D('metro',{etymology:E('Shortened from metropolitan, first used for an urban railway; metro also shortens metropolitan area for a large city and its connected towns.','metro'),contexts:[C('metro.s1','交通','We took the metro across town and changed trains at the central station.','我们坐地铁穿过城区，并在中央车站换了车。','take the metro names riding the urban railway; across town gives the route.','Metro is a count noun for the railway system or its trains; it usually takes the in this sense.','This is the urban-railway sense; metro can also mean a large city with joined towns.')],mistakes:[M('They took the metropolis from the airport to the hotel.','They took the metro from the airport to the hotel.','Metropolis means a large city; metro is the railway or train used for the journey.','confusable')],quiz:[Q('metro',1,1,'What does “take the metro” mean?','Travel on an urban railway system.','Travel by meteorite.','Study a city’s weather.','Travel on an urban railway system.','Metro commonly names an underground or urban railway and its trains.'),Q('metro',2,2,'In regional use, a city’s metro may include …','the large city and the towns joined to it.','only the tunnels under one street.','a single weather station.','the large city and the towns joined to it.','Metro can also refer to a major city together with its connected towns.'),Q('metro',3,1,'Which sentence uses metro for transport?','The metro runs every six minutes.','The metro includes the suburbs and nearby towns.','The metro of the island is hard to predict.','The metro runs every six minutes.','A railway system or its trains can run at regular intervals.'),Q('metro',4,1,'A traveler buys a ticket at an underground station. The ticket is for the …','metro.','metropolis.','metrology.','metro.','Metro is the urban rail service; metropolis names a major city.') ]});
