D('miasmic',{etymology:E('From miasma + -ic; miasma came through Greek miasma “pollution, defilement,” from miainein “to stain or pollute.”','miasma'),contexts:[C('miasmic.s1','文学','A miasmic fog clung to the marsh, carrying the smell of stagnant water.','一层瘴气般的浓雾笼罩着沼泽，带着死水的气味。','miasmic modifies fog and describes thick, unhealthy vapour.','Miasmic is an adjective; it can also describe a poisonous or oppressive atmosphere figuratively.','The sentence uses the literal vapour sense; it does not claim that the fog contains a specific poison.')],mistakes:[M('The clear mountain air felt miasmic and healthy.','The clear mountain air felt fresh and healthy.','Miasmic describes unhealthy, foul vapour or a poisonous atmosphere, so clear healthy air is not miasmic.','meaning')],quiz:[Q('miasmic',1,1,'A miasmic fog is …','thick, unhealthy, and foul-smelling.','clear and refreshing.','a small electronic circuit.','thick, unhealthy, and foul-smelling.','Miasmic relates to a miasma: unhealthy vapour or a foul atmosphere.'),Q('miasmic',2,1,'Which scene best fits miasmic?','A poisonous haze hangs over a stagnant marsh.','A clean breeze crosses a bright field.','A quiet library has fresh air.','A poisonous haze hangs over a stagnant marsh.','An unhealthy, oppressive haze is aptly described as miasmic.'),Q('miasmic',3,1,'In a figurative description, a miasmic atmosphere feels …','poisonous or oppressive.','cheerful and celebratory.','carefully measured in metres.','poisonous or oppressive.','The word can describe a harmful or oppressive figurative atmosphere.'),Q('miasmic',4,1,'Which adjective is closest to miasmic in a literal fog description?','foul and unhealthy','sunlit and crisp','metallic and solid','foul and unhealthy','Miasmic points to unhealthy vapour rather than fresh air or a solid material.') ]});
